  "answer": "According to the Camelid Support Escalation Guide \n[1]\n, if a security incident affects customer data, the account owner will be notified within seventy-two hours of confirmation, with a written summary of scope and remediation \n[1]\n. However, the guide does not explicitly state when the customer will be informed of the breach.\n\nThe guide does mention that the security team will review the suspected data breach within one hour of the report, but it does not provide a timeline for informing the customer \n[2]\n. Additionally, the support policy states that the account owner will be notified within seventy-two hours, but it does not specify when the customer will be informed of the breach \n[3]\n.\n\nIt appears that the customer will not be informed of the breach immediately, but rather within a certain timeframe. However, the exact timeline is not specified in the provided excerpts.\n\nReferences\n\n[1]\n Camelid Support Escalation Guide, Version 1.3\n\n[2]\n Camelid Support Escalation Guide, Version 1.3\n\n[3]\n Support Policy, Version 1.3\n\nLlama 3.2 3B Instruct Q4_K_M\nVERIFIED\ntokens in 372 · out 216\nfirst token 5.4s\n55 tok/s\n9.3s\n10:44 AM\nCLIENT-MEASURED\nDeveloper Diagnostics\n55.0 tok/s",
